  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "05. Attack Sequence",
    "ruleNumber": "05.00",
    "summary": "Attacks are settled with the attack sequence, which decides whether each one inflicts damage. Whenever the [active player](vsdata:core-rule/active-player-and-opposing-player) is told to resolve it, they go through four numbered steps in order: **[Hit Rolls](vsdata:core-rule/hit-rolls)** (05.01), **[Wound Rolls](vsdata:core-rule/wound-rolls)** (05.02), **[Save Rolls](vsdata:core-rule/save-rolls)** (05.03) and **[Inflict Damage](vsdata:core-rule/inflict-damage)** (05.04). Inside a step, every die that step calls for is rolled together. Each attack leaves the sequence as soon as it either fails or inflicts damage, and when every attack has done one or the other, they all count as resolved. A side panel adds that a critical hit still counts as a hit and a critical wound as a wound, and that some weapon abilities, among them [[LETHAL HITS]](vsdata:weapon-ability/lethal-hits) and [[DEVASTATING WOUNDS]](vsdata:weapon-ability/devastating-wounds), key off those results.",
